From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: diaaney <latte@diane.zip>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 23:45:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rapier - 1.8 combat: blockhit consume time 2s so the eat pose
 actually plays

the first-person eat transform scales with consume progress
(1 - remainingFraction^27) and the chew wobble only starts after 20%
consumed. with a 36000s duration the progress never left ~0 and the
sword barely moved. 2.0s raises the sword to the face within ~4 ticks;
while the button is held the client seamlessly re-triggers the consume
in a loop, and the finishUsingItem guard keeps the sword from ever
being consumed.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/item/ToolMaterial.java b/net/minecraft/world/item/ToolMaterial.java
index 1e6cbbd7c60351317fe7a52a586022de09bd81eb..f0a971800c0b19889f9e941346fa8469f6ed1086 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/item/ToolMaterial.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/item/ToolMaterial.java
@@ -104,14 +104,16 @@ public record ToolMaterial(
                 )
             )
             // rapier - 1.8 combat: CONSUMABLE drives the client-side render pose. modern clients removed the 1.8 sword
-            // blocking pose and render BLOCKS_ATTACKS with the shield brace (sword held flat); the EAT use-animation is
-            // the closest match to the classic raised blockhit look. consume time is absurd so it never completes,
-            // sound is intentionally_empty and particles off so no eating audio/crumbs. server logic still uses the
-            // BLOCKS_ATTACKS path in Item.use (the consumable branch skips blockhit swords).
+            // blocking pose, so the EAT use-animation is the closest match to the classic raised blockhit look.
+            // the eat pose intensity is progress-based (1 - remainingFraction^27), so the consume time must be SHORT
+            // for the raise to actually play: 2.0s raises the sword within ~4 ticks and wobbles near the face; while
+            // the button stays held the client re-triggers the consume seamlessly in a loop. the sword itself is never
+            // consumed (Item.finishUsingItem guard). sound is intentionally_empty and particles off, so no eating
+            // audio or crumbs. blocking mechanics stay on the server via BLOCKS_ATTACKS, which is never sent to clients.
             .component(
                 DataComponents.CONSUMABLE,
                 new net.minecraft.world.item.component.Consumable(
-                    36000.0F,
+                    2.0F,
                     net.minecraft.world.item.ItemUseAnimation.EAT,
                     net.minecraft.core.registries.BuiltInRegistries.SOUND_EVENT.wrapAsHolder(net.minecraft.sounds.SoundEvents.EMPTY),
                     false,
